; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR SNAKE  -  eat, grow, don't bite the wall or yourself   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load, cold-boot, press SPACE. Arrow keys (or w a s d) steer the snake to the
; food '*'; each one eaten scores 1 and makes the snake 3 longer, and every 4 the
; game gets faster (levels 0-9). Running into a wall or your own body ends the
; game. P pauses, ESC quits; SPACE plays again. BEST is kept while it runs.
;
; The body is the grid itself: each cell remembers which way the snake left it,
; and the tail follows those arrows - no segment list, no length limit.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing, erase to end of line, hide/show cursor. No scrolling.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/snake_verify.py, V0061.34): ALL PASS 2026-09-28 - autopilot to level 9 on 3 seeds with the screen and grid checked every step; wall; bite; straight-back ignored; two queued turns; 120/120 arrows turned the snake with the 1-byte UART overrunning; pause; restart; quit; rerun without reload
; HW-VERIFIED on the Elf2K (V0061.34), 2026-09-28 - Craig: "Snake works as well."
;
; 387 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
